WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.079 --> 00:00:05.819
Mourning the victims, and searching for answers
in Christchurch.

00:00:05.819 --> 00:00:11.019
Outside the city's al-Noor Mosque, people
paused to honor those who lost their lives

00:00:11.019 --> 00:00:17.820
in the worst mass murder in New Zealand's
modern history.

00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:23.029
These were the scenes Friday, as a suspected
white supremacist opened fire on worshippers

00:00:23.029 --> 00:00:28.980
at al-Noor, and at a Mosque in the neighborhood
of Linwood, killing and wounding dozens.

00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:34.300
As police scrambled to stop the shooter, rescuers
raced to save the wounded.

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:40.630
Survivors spoke of a narrow escape.

00:00:40.630 --> 00:00:47.430
After three or four minutes we heard you know,
the firing, and it was from the main entrance,

00:00:47.430 --> 00:00:53.619
the main entrance of the building, and then
everybody just run towards the back doors

00:00:53.619 --> 00:00:56.370
just to save themselves.

00:00:56.370 --> 00:01:03.439
First we hide behind cars, you know under
the car, and we see the firing still on we

00:01:03.439 --> 00:01:06.860
tried to jump the fence.

00:01:06.860 --> 00:01:12.600
This footage shows the moment police apprehended
the suspect, after forcing his car off the

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:20.500
road; they brought an end to the rampage.

00:01:20.500 --> 00:01:25.360
The suspected shooter is 28-year-old Australian
Brenton Tarrant.

00:01:25.360 --> 00:01:30.340
Charged with murder, he appeared for the first
time in court on Saturday and was remanded

00:01:30.340 --> 00:01:33.150
to custody until April 5.

00:01:33.150 --> 00:01:39.560
Investigators say he published a racist, anti-immigrant
'Manifesto' online before carrying out the

00:01:39.560 --> 00:01:40.980
massacre.

00:01:40.980 --> 00:01:45.690
Prime Minister Jacinda Ardern vowed to tighten
the country's gun laws, after it was revealed

00:01:45.690 --> 00:01:49.800
Tarrant had a license to carry the types of
guns used in the attack.

00:01:49.800 --> 00:01:54.700
"While work is being done as to the chain
of events that led to both the holding of

00:01:54.700 --> 00:02:00.470
this gun license, and the possession of these
weapons, I can tell you one thing right now

00:02:00.470 --> 00:02:03.470
- our gun laws will change."

00:02:03.470 --> 00:02:09.940
After the attack, New Zealand's terror alert
level was raised from low to high, with added

00:02:09.940 --> 00:02:12.790
security around the country's Mosques.

00:02:12.790 --> 00:02:16.000
Dozens of the wounded remain hospitalized,
some of whom are still

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:19.000
fighting for their lives.

